// uaf-bug: the use-after-free program of programs/uaf-bug-rc11.lit.
//
// RC11z makes allocation and deallocation writes to the memory they allocate or
//   free, ordered by co with the stores to it. That changes the coherence
//   orders the executions are admitted under, not the verdict.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     RC11z forbids. RC11z coincides with RC11 on the concurrency behaviours of
//       programs (zoo edge RC11 = RC11z).
//   the models' definitions:
//     RC11 forbids. The program's reference verdict under RC11: the relacq
//       fence synchronises the free with the load of the freed cell, as
//       programs/uaf-bug-rc11.lit asserts.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: SC, VbD, TSO,
//     x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence, RC17, OD-LSO, MRD, CC, PC, PRAM, Causal,
//     Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, MW, WFR. RA, SRA and WRA are defined on
//     release stores and acquire loads, and this program has other accesses.
rC := malloc(1);
*rC := 0;
rcu := malloc(1);
*rcu := 1;
fence(relacq);
{
  rtemp := *rcu;
  if (rtemp = 0) {
    free(rC);
  }
}
|||
{
  rv := *rC;
  *rcu := 0;
}
%%
forbid (ub) [RC11, RC11z]
